.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt NVIDIA-FIRMWARE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvidia-firmware
.Nd place the GSP firmware the NVIDIA GPUs of the machine need into /boot
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm detect
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl -no-delete
.Op Fl -keep-versions
.Op Fl -expect-card
.Op Fl -version Ar version
.Nm
.Cm list
.Op Fl -cards
.Nm
.Cm status
.Nm
.Cm verify
.Nm
.Cm install
.Op Fl n
.Fl -force Ar image
.Op Fl -version Ar version
.Nm
.Cm install
.Op Fl n
.Fl -all
.Op Fl -version Ar version
.Nm
.Cm remove
.Op Fl n
.Ar image
.Nm
.Cm clean
.Op Fl n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
places the NVIDIA GSP firmware that the graphics adapters of the machine
need into
.Pa /boot/firmware/nvidia .
The firmware itself comes from the
.Nm nvidia-firmware
package, which holds one directory per driver version under
.Pa /usr/local/share/nvidia-firmware .
Each of those directories holds the images of that version, a
.Pa SHA256SUMS
file with the hash of every image and the
.Pa supported-gpus.json
file that names the chips the driver knows.
.Pp
The options
.Fl -libxo Ar json
and
.Fl -json
write the output as JSON instead of text.
.Fl -json
is an alias for
.Fl -libxo Ar json .
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm detect
Find the NVIDIA graphics adapters of the machine and place into
.Pa /boot/firmware/nvidia
exactly the images those adapters need.
The version used is the one given with
.Fl -version ,
else the version the
.Vt hw.nvidia.version_pin
sysctl names when that version is installed, else the newest installed
version.
Only the images that
.Nm
placed itself are ever removed, and only when no adapter present needs them
and they are not forced.
A file in the directory that is not named in
.Pa SHA256SUMS
belongs to somebody else; it is reported as foreign and left alone.
.Pp
With
.Fl -no-delete
nothing is removed.
The same effect comes from
.Va nvidia_firmware_no_delete=YES
in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
or
.Pa /etc/rc.conf.d/nvidia_firmware .
Those two files are read with the same simple
.Nm name Ns = Ns Ar value
lines
.Xr rc 8
uses; no other syntax is understood.
.Pp
With
.Fl -keep-versions
the images of an older version stay in place.
Without it the images of the older version are removed once the images of
the version that is going to load are in place.
.Pp
With
.Fl -expect-card
the command fails when the machine has no NVIDIA graphics adapter.
Without it the command places nothing, removes the images that are not
needed and succeeds.
.It Cm list
List every installed version and every image of it: the size of the image,
the chip families it serves, the products of those families the version
knows about, whether the driver reaches that hardware today, and whether
the image is placed in
.Pa /boot/firmware/nvidia
and for which adapter.
.Pp
With
.Fl -cards
only the graphics adapters of the machine are listed: the PCI selector, the
device id, the name NVIDIA gives the chip in
.Pa supported-gpus.json ,
the family of the chip and the images it needs for every installed
version.
The list works when the firmware is not installed: the adapters are listed
and the tool says that the firmware is not installed.
.It Cm status
Show what is in
.Pa /boot/firmware/nvidia :
the size and the version of every image, the adapter each image serves, the
images that are forced and whether the no-delete setting is on.
.It Cm verify
Check every installed version of the share directory against its
.Pa SHA256SUMS
file and the files in
.Pa /boot/firmware/nvidia
against the
.Pa SHA256SUMS
file there.
A file that was changed, a file that is missing and a file of ours that
the inventory does not name are errors.
A foreign file is reported but is not an error.
.It Cm install
Place an image that no adapter needs and mark it forced.
.Fl -force Ar image
places one image of the version, and
.Fl -all
places every image of the version.
.It Cm remove Ar image
Remove an image from
.Pa /boot/firmware/nvidia
and drop its forced mark.
The image is gone at once; it is not left for the next
.Cm detect .
.Pp
The command refuses to run while the loaded driver uses the image: unload
the nvidia module first.
A file that the
.Pa SHA256SUMS
file of the directory does not name belongs to somebody else and is never
removed.
When a card of the machine needs the image, the command warns about it and
removes it anyway.
.It Cm clean
Remove every image
.Nm
placed in
.Pa /boot/firmware/nvidia .
The command refuses to run while the nvidia kernel module is loaded.
.El
.Pp
Every command that changes something accepts
.Fl n ,
which prints what the command would do and changes nothing.
.Pp
Every command that changes the boot directory refuses to run while the
nvidia kernel module is loaded, and refuses to run when it cannot tell
whether the module is loaded: the tool does not change the firmware of a
driver that is in use and does not guess.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NVIDIA_FIRMWARE_TEST_ROOT
.It Ev NVIDIA_FIRMWARE_TEST_PCI
.It Ev NVIDIA_FIRMWARE_TEST_KLD
.It Ev NVIDIA_FIRMWARE_TEST_PIN
These variables belong to the test suite of the program.
They are ignored unless the program was built for the test suite, and the
installed program ignores them in every case.
.It Ev NVIDIA_FIRMWARE_TEST_ROOT
The root of a fake system.
The share directory, the boot directory and the two files of
.Xr rc 8
are looked for below it.
.It Ev NVIDIA_FIRMWARE_TEST_PCI
A file of device ids, one per line, that takes the place of the scan of the
PCI bus.
A line may name the PCI selector of the card after the device id.
.It Ev NVIDIA_FIRMWARE_TEST_KLD
The word
.Ql loaded
or
.Ql not
for the state of the nvidia kernel module.
.It Ev NVIDIA_FIRMWARE_TEST_PIN
The version the
.Vt hw.nvidia.version_pin
sysctl would name.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /boot/firmware/nvidia/SHA256SUMS" -compact
.It Pa /boot/firmware/nvidia
The directory the firmware is placed in.
.It Pa /boot/firmware/nvidia/SHA256SUMS
The inventory of that directory.
Every line names one image:
.Pp
.Dl sha256  image  version  forced  size
.Pp
The hash is the one of the image in the share directory, the version is the
driver version it came from, the fourth field is
.Ql forced
for an image that
.Cm install
placed and a dash for any other image, and the last field is the size of
the image in bytes.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/nvidia-firmware
The directory the package installs the firmware into.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/nvidia-firmware/nvidia-firmware.families
The table that says which chip family a PCI device id belongs to and which
images each driver version needs for that family.
The program holds the same table inside itself, so that it can name the
family of a card when the firmware is not installed.
.It Pa /etc/rc.conf
.It Pa /etc/rc.conf.d/nvidia_firmware
The files that hold the
.Va nvidia_firmware_no_delete
setting.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
The command did what it was asked to do.
.It 1
The command failed.
.It 2
The command was used wrongly.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Place the firmware the adapters of the machine need:
.Pp
.Dl $ nvidia-firmware detect
.Pp
See what would be placed, without touching anything:
.Pp
.Dl $ nvidia-firmware detect -n
.Pp
Place the firmware of a version that is not the newest one:
.Pp
.Dl $ nvidia-firmware detect --version 580.178.04
.Pp
Write the list of the images as JSON:
.Pp
.Dl $ nvidia-firmware list --libxo json
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldstat 8 ,
.Xr rc 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
